Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their potential usage and key conditions  
• week_date (cleaned_weekly_sales): used to isolate the 24‑week window (12 weeks before and 12 weeks after 2020‑06‑15).  
• sales (cleaned_weekly_sales): metric whose percentage change will be compared.  
• region (cleaned_weekly_sales): attribute #1 for which the average % change will be calculated.  
• platform (cleaned_weekly_sales): attribute #2.  
• age_band (cleaned_weekly_sales): attribute #3.  
• demographic (cleaned_weekly_sales): attribute #4.  
• customer_type (cleaned_weekly_sales): attribute #5.  
• calendar_year, week_number, month_number (cleaned_weekly_sales): optional helpers for filtering or sanity checks.

Typical conditions that may be used  
• week_date BETWEEN '2020-03-23' AND '2020-06-14'  -- 12 weeks before 15‑Jun‑2020  
• week_date BETWEEN '2020-06-15' AND '2020-09-07'  -- 12 weeks after 15‑Jun‑2020  
(Alternatively filter by week_number / calendar_year if preferred.)

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Exploratory SQL queries
-----------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1) Inspect the weekly dates available around the period of interest
SELECT DISTINCT week_date
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
WHERE week_date BETWEEN '2020-03-01' AND '2020-09-30'
ORDER BY week_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Quick look at total sales by week to make sure data exist on both sides of 15‑Jun‑2020
SELECT week_date,
       SUM(sales) AS total_sales
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
WHERE week_date BETWEEN '2020-03-23' AND '2020-09-07'
GROUP BY week_date
ORDER BY week_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Distinct list of regions that will be part of the region‑level change calculation
SELECT DISTINCT region
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Distinct list of platforms
SELECT DISTINCT platform
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Distinct list of age bands
SELECT DISTINCT age_band
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Distinct list of demographics
SELECT DISTINCT demographic
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Distinct list of customer types
SELECT DISTINCT customer_type
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Aggregate sales before and after 15‑Jun‑2020 per region (step toward % change)
SELECT region,
       SUM(CASE WHEN week_date <  '2020-06-15' THEN sales END) AS sales_before,
       SUM(CASE WHEN week_date >= '2020-06-15' THEN sales END) AS sales_after
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
WHERE week_date BETWEEN '2020-03-23' AND '2020-09-07'
GROUP BY region
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Aggregate sales before and after per platform
SELECT platform,
       SUM(CASE WHEN week_date <  '2020-06-15' THEN sales END) AS sales_before,
       SUM(CASE WHEN week_date >= '2020-06-15' THEN sales END) AS sales_after
FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
WHERE week_date BETWEEN '2020-03-23' AND '2020-09-07'
GROUP BY platform
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) One‑shot query computing the average % change across all values
--     for each attribute type; this will allow spotting the biggest negative impact
WITH windowed AS (
    SELECT *,
           CASE WHEN week_date < '2020-06-15' THEN 'before' ELSE 'after' END AS period
    FROM cleaned_weekly_sales
    WHERE week_date BETWEEN '2020-03-23' AND '2020-09-07'
), sums AS (
    -- sales_before and sales_after for every value of every attribute type
    SELECT region               AS attribute_value, 'region'       AS attribute_type,
           SUM(CASE WHEN period='before' THEN sales END) AS sales_before,
           SUM(CASE WHEN period='after'  THEN sales END) AS sales_after
    FROM windowed GROUP BY region
    UNION ALL
    SELECT platform             AS attribute_value, 'platform',     SUM(CASE WHEN period='before' THEN sales END), SUM(CASE WHEN period='after' THEN sales END)
    FROM windowed GROUP BY platform
    UNION ALL
    SELECT age_band             AS attribute_value, 'age_band',     SUM(CASE WHEN period='before' THEN sales END), SUM(CASE WHEN period='after' THEN sales END)
    FROM windowed GROUP BY age_band
    UNION ALL
    SELECT demographic          AS attribute_value, 'demographic',  SUM(CASE WHEN period='before' THEN sales END), SUM(CASE WHEN period='after' THEN sales END)
    FROM windowed GROUP BY demographic
    UNION ALL
    SELECT customer_type        AS attribute_value, 'customer_type',SUM(CASE WHEN period='before' THEN sales END), SUM(CASE WHEN period='after' THEN sales END)
    FROM windowed GROUP BY customer_type
), pct_change AS (
    SELECT attribute_type,
           AVG(
               (sales_after - sales_before) * 1.0 / NULLIF(sales_before,0)
           ) AS avg_pct_change
    FROM sums
    GROUP BY attribute_type
)
SELECT *
FROM pct_change
ORDER BY avg_pct_change     -- most negative at top
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query surfaces the average percentage change in sales for each of the five attribute types and orders them so you can immediately identify which one had the greatest negative impact.
